::callout{type="warning"}
When I changed line 43 to `tuple(assigned_selector) in variable_selectors` locally, both streaming tests passed. I then reverted that local change.

::suggestion{file="api/core/workflow/nodes/variable_assigner/v1/node.py" lines="42-43"}
        assigned_selector = tuple(self.node_data.assigned_variable_selector)
        return assigned_selector in variable_selectors

The PR adds a branch in `_run` so the result's `inputs['value']` is `updated_variable.to_object()` for CLEAR and `income_value.to_object()` otherwise. For CLEAR, `updated_variable` was built with `value = income_value.to_object()`, where `income_value` is the zero value. So both expressions give the same object, and the branch does nothing functionally. It also isn't related to the streaming fix in the PR title or description, and no test covers it.

If it's intentional, a comment or test should say why. Otherwise it's noise that a reviewer has to reason through.

