The new import `from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Set, Tuple` and the annotation `Set[Tuple[str, ...]]` use the deprecated `typing` aliases. The sibling implementations use builtin generics: `base/node.py` (line 435) and `variable_assigner/v2/node.py` (line 70) both write `set[tuple[str, ...]]`. Linters with the pyupgrade (`UP`) rules flag `typing.Set`/`Tuple`. I didn't run ruff here (it isn't on the PATH in this environment), so this is from reading the code.

